/T (A computer analyses an image as a matrix of pixels, and then uses algorithms to group the pixels into categories. The algorithm extracts features from the image, such as edges, textures, or shapes, to determine the most appropriate label. Image classification is a supervised learning problem, where a model is trained to recognize a set of target classes using labelled example photos. mage classification is a fundamental project in computer vision that provides valuable data and insights for informed decisions. Deep learning algorithms, such as CNNs, are commonly used for image classification. A well-optimized classification dataset is important for accurate results. Publicly available datasets are often used for training. A trained model's accuracy and precision scores are evaluated on a test set. )
